From d2c75f7c8d251b06a7356fea4efafcf3c9c2daaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zak Wilson <zak.wilson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:48:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] An element under a macro call is still a place

(ref ((aref ((uvalue o) 'uv) i) 'uv)) still copied: the receiver was an
aref, not a field form. emit-untyped-receiver expands a macro at the
receiver's head and takes the address of any field, aref or deref
form; set!'s last-resort receiver uses it too. Found by the nuc-lua
port (its ISSUE-043, lua_setiuservalue).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CsC8i2S7yJAHSpzRaddMj3
